{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Not with our fathers</b> alone <b>did He cut the covenant, but with us, we</b> — analogy: 'Your name shall no longer be called Jacob, but Israel' — not alone, but with him. As is stated in Midrash Tehillim regarding 'From the mouths of babes and sucklings You have founded strength' — that even the fetuses in their mothers' wombs accepted the Torah and served as guarantors for their fathers to accept the Torah, and their mothers' wombs became transparent like glass, and they were seen and saw the face of the Shekhinah. And when HaShem says 'I am HaShem,' they answer after Him: yes. 'You shall not have' — and they answer after Him: no. And so for every positive: yes, and for every negative: no." "<b>But with us, we.</b> Even though there are now among us many people who were born afterward and were not present at the standing of that covenant, nevertheless the written covenant applies to them, as it is written: 'visiting the iniquity of fathers upon children and upon children's children, upon the third and upon the fourth generation, and doing kindness to thousands' etc. An analogy to this is written in the portion Nitzavim: 'and not with you alone do I cut this covenant.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:46.724220216Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}